## Concurrent Trie (RCU‑Based Prefix Tree)

### 1. Overview
The goal is to provide **lock‑free reads** for routing lookups while allowing **safe concurrent updates** (insert/delete). We achieve this by:
- Storing each trie node in an RCU‑protected list.
- Using `rcu_read_lock()` / `rcu_read_unlock()` for readers.
- Updating nodes under a write lock and then calling `synchronize_rcu()` to wait for all pre‑existing readers to finish before freeing the old node.

### 2. Data Structure
```c
/* Node definition – contains children and optional leaf flag */
struct rcu_node {
    struct list_head children;   /* RCU protected list of child nodes */
    bool leaf;                    /* true if this node terminates a prefix */
    struct rcu_head rcu;         /* deferred free */
};
```
All nodes are allocated with `kmalloc()` and linked via `list_add()`/`list_del()`.

### 3. Insertion Algorithm (Writer)
```c
void rcu_trie_insert(const unsigned char *prefix,
                    size_t len,
                    const void *data,
                    size_t data_len)
{
    struct rcu_node *root = NULL;
    struct rcu_node *tmp = NULL;
    struct rcu_node *new = NULL;
    LIST(trie) head, tmp2;

    /* Allocate new node lazily in bulk */
    tmp2.next = NULL;
    tmp2.prev = NULL;
    tmp2.next->next = NULL;
    tmp2.prev->prev = NULL;

    spinlock(&trielock);
    spinlock(&trielock);

    /* Bulk allocation of intermediate nodes */
    for (size_t i = 0; i < len; ++i) {
        unsigned char c = prefix[i];
        if (!root) root = newlist();
        if (!new) new = newlist();
        list_add(&new->rcu, &tmp->next);
        tmp->next->next = NULL;
        tmp->prev->prev = &tmp->next;
        tmp->next = &new->rcu;
        new->leaf = false;
        new->children.next = NULL;
        new->children.prev = NULL;
        new->children.next = NULL;
        new->children.prev = NULL;
        new->children.next = NULL;
        new->children.prev = NULL;
        new->children.next = NULL;
        new->children.prev = NULL;
        new->children.next = NULL;
        new->children.prev = NULL;
        new->children.next = NULL;
        new->children.prev = NULL;
        new->children.next = NULL;
        new->children.prev = NULL;

        spinlock(&trielock);
    }

    /* Insert leaf flag */
    if (!root) root = &new[0];
    else {
        struct rcu_node *cur =
            list_entry(root, struct rcu_node, children);
        while (*len > 0 && cur) {
