    let rc = MyRc::from(x);

    // Dereference safely – no double‑free because Drop runs when rc goes out of scope.
    println!("value = {}", *rc);
}
```
The example demonstrates how ownership works: after printing, Rust drops `rc`, invoking our custom destructor which calls `dec_ref`. When the last owner disappears, our manual decrement frees the underlying memory exactly once.

